# ICCP / TASE.2 server (not in stock bennu: there is no oracle, so DUT defaults to rust). server.xml is one bilateral-table row (EMS1,
# any address) over a brkr, a load MW, a bus voltage, a command state and a setpoint. There is no open ICCP peer: libiec61850's
# mms_utility (a generic MMS client) browses and reads it, and our own thin client (examples/iccp-client, built by cargo test) does
# the TASE.2 part (write, data set, transfer set, InformationReport); it is copied into the peers container (PEER_BIN).
# Listens on 127.0.0.1:102.
CFG=${CFG:-${here:-/conformance}/${proto:-iccp}/server.xml}
DUT_DEFAULT=rust
DUT_CAPS=''
PEER_BIN=target-linux/debug/examples/iccp-client
STOCK_CMD='echo "bennu has no ICCP server: run with DUT=rust" >&2; exit 2'
WARMUP=4
CAPTURE_FILTER='tcp port 102'
PROTO_FILTER='mms'
EXPERT_ALLOW='D-SACK Sequence'
ZEEK_LOAD=''
